        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Task 2 — `expression_landscape`\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question:** how does your gene's expression vary across cancer types?\n",
        "\n",
        "This is context. Before testing anything you want to know whether your\n",
        "gene is switched on at all in your tumour type, or whether you are about\n",
        "to run statistics on noise.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Takes** `expr` — the tidy expression table.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns** a DataFrame of **tumour samples only**, one row per cancer\n",
        "type:\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "cancer_type, n, median_log2tpm\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Sorted by `median_log2tpm`, **highest first**, index reset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "S8JvPbxp9GM9"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def expression_landscape(expr):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Summarise the gene's expression across cancer types.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Use tumour samples to calculate the sample count and median\n",
        "    log2 expression for each cancer type, then rank the cancer types\n",
        "    from the highest median expression to the lowest.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    # Restrict the landscape to tumours so normal samples do not affect the cancer-type summaries.\n",
        "    tumours = expr[expr[\"group\"] == \"tumour\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Summarise each cancer type by its number of tumour samples and median expression.\n",
        "    landscape = tumours.groupby(\"cancer_type\").agg(\n",
        "        n=(\"log2_tpm\", \"size\"),\n",
        "        median_log2tpm=(\"log2_tpm\", \"median\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Put cancer_type back into the table as a column, then rank cancers by median expression.\n",
        "    landscape = landscape.reset_index()\n",
        "    landscape = landscape.sort_values(\n",
        "        \"median_log2tpm\",\n",
        "        ascending=False,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Give the ranked table a consecutive index for a clear, reproducible output.\n",
        "    landscape = landscape.reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return landscape[[\"cancer_type\", \"n\", \"median_log2tpm\"]]\n",
        "    raise NotImplementedError(\"expression_landscape\")"
      ]
    },
