        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Task 3 — `compare_groups`\n",
        "\n",
        "Now the actual question. You run the **same test twice**, on two\n",
        "different splits:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Tumour vs normal**, within your cancer type — is the gene\n",
        "   dysregulated in cancer at all?\n",
        "2. **TP53-mutant vs wild-type**, within the tumours — **does it respond\n",
        "   to p53 loss?**\n",
        "\n",
        "### Write one function, not two\n",
        "\n",
        "These two comparisons do the same arithmetic on different columns.\n",
        "Writing `compare_tumour_normal` and `compare_tp53` as two near-identical\n",
        "functions is the commonest way to lose code-quality marks here.\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "compare_groups(expr, group_col, group_a, group_b)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "**Takes** `expr`, a tidy expression table already filtered to the rows\n",
        "you want to compare; `group_col`, the column holding the group labels;\n",
        "and `group_a` and `group_b`, the two labels to compare.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns** a dict with exactly these keys:\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "{\"n_a\": int, \"n_b\": int, \"median_a\": float, \"median_b\": float,\n",
        " \"difference\": float, \"p_value\": float, \"significant\": bool}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "`difference` is `median_a - median_b`. `significant` is\n",
        "`p_value < 0.05`. The test is a **two-sided Mann–Whitney U**\n",
        "(`scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu`), and rows with a missing `log2_tpm` or a\n",
        "missing group label are dropped.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Why Mann–Whitney and not a t-test\n",
        "\n",
        "Expression data is not normally distributed — it is skewed, and a few\n",
        "tumours express enormously more than the rest. Mann–Whitney compares\n",
        "**ranks**, so it assumes no shape and one extreme tumour cannot drag the\n",
        "result. That is also why you report **medians**, not means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4vKWeEoP9GM-"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def compare_groups(expr, group_col, group_a, group_b):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Compare expression between two labelled groups.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Exclude rows missing the expression value or group label, then\n",
        "    compare the groups' medians with a two-sided Mann–Whitney U test.\n",
        "    The reported difference is the median in group A minus the median\n",
        "    in group B.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    # Exclude incomplete rows before calculating group summaries or running the test.\n",
        "    comparison_data = expr[[group_col, \"log2_tpm\"]].dropna()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Select expression values for the two groups specified by the caller.\n",
        "    values_a = comparison_data[\n",
        "        comparison_data[group_col] == group_a\n",
        "    ][\"log2_tpm\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    values_b = comparison_data[\n",
        "        comparison_data[group_col] == group_b\n",
        "    ][\"log2_tpm\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Record each group's sample size and median; the sign of the difference\n",
        "    # indicates whether the median is higher in group A or group B.\n",
        "    n_a = len(values_a)\n",
        "    n_b = len(values_b)\n",
        "    median_a = float(values_a.median())\n",
        "    median_b = float(values_b.median())\n",
        "    difference = median_a - median_b\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Use a two-sided test to assess whether expression distributions differ\n",
        "    # without specifying the direction in advance.\n",
        "    test_result = mannwhitneyu(\n",
        "        values_a,\n",
        "        values_b,\n",
        "        alternative=\"two-sided\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    p_value = float(test_result.pvalue)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Apply the project's 0.05 significance threshold and return the\n",
        "    # sample sizes, effect summary and test result together.\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"n_a\": n_a,\n",
        "        \"n_b\": n_b,\n",
        "        \"median_a\": median_a,\n",
        "        \"median_b\": median_b,\n",
        "        \"difference\": difference,\n",
        "        \"p_value\": p_value,\n",
        "        \"significant\": p_value < 0.05,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    raise NotImplementedError(\"compare_groups\")"
      ]
    },
