        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Pulling it together — `run_analysis`\n",
        "\n",
        "One function that runs the whole analysis and returns the answer.\n",
        "**Each key is marked separately**, so a key you cannot produce costs you\n",
        "that key and nothing else.\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "run_analysis(expression_path, gene, cancer_type)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "**Takes** `expression_path`, the path to the tidy expression CSV;\n",
        "`gene`; and `cancer_type`.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Returns**:\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "{\"gene\": str, \"cancer_type\": str, \"n_samples\": int,\n",
        " \"landscape_top\": str,          # cancer type with the highest median\n",
        " \"tumour_vs_normal\": {...},     # a compare_groups dict\n",
        " \"tp53\": {...},                 # a compare_groups dict\n",
        " \"verdict\": \"down\" | \"up\" | \"no change\"}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "`verdict` follows from the TP53 comparison: not significant →\n",
        "`\"no change\"`; `difference` below zero → `\"down\"`; above zero → `\"up\"`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Note it takes **only** the expression file. Notebook 01 is not part of\n",
        "this — it stands on its own, and nothing here can be blocked by it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 13,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PlE26pkD9GM_"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def run_analysis(expression_path, gene, cancer_type):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Run the expression analysis for one gene and cancer type.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Read the tidy expression data, summarise the expression landscape,\n",
        "    compare tumour with normal samples and compare TP53-mutant with\n",
        "    wild-type tumours. Return the comparisons and the verdict.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    # Load the tidy expression table used for both the landscape and comparisons.\n",
        "    expression_data = pd.read_csv(expression_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Restrict the group comparisons to the assigned cancer type.\n",
        "    cancer_data = expression_data[\n",
        "        expression_data[\"cancer_type\"] == cancer_type\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    tumour_data = cancer_data[cancer_data[\"group\"] == \"tumour\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Identify the cancer type with the highest median tumour expression.\n",
        "    landscape = expression_landscape(expression_data)\n",
        "    landscape_top = landscape[\"cancer_type\"][0]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # First compare tumour with normal tissue within the assigned cancer type.\n",
        "    tumour_vs_normal = compare_groups(\n",
        "        cancer_data,\n",
        "        \"group\",\n",
        "        \"tumour\",\n",
        "        \"normal\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Then compare TP53-mutant with wild-type tumours in the same cancer type.\n",
        "    tp53 = compare_groups(\n",
        "        tumour_data,\n",
        "        \"tp53_status\",\n",
        "        \"MUT\",\n",
        "        \"WT\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Report no change when the comparison is not significant or the\n",
        "    # median difference is zero; otherwise use its sign to set the direction.\n",
        "    if not tp53[\"significant\"] or tp53[\"difference\"] == 0:\n",
        "        verdict = \"no change\"\n",
        "    elif tp53[\"difference\"] < 0:\n",
        "        verdict = \"down\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        verdict = \"up\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Return the assigned context, landscape result and both comparisons\n",
        "    # alongside the verdict derived from the TP53 comparison.\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"gene\": gene,\n",
        "        \"cancer_type\": cancer_type,\n",
        "        \"n_samples\": len(cancer_data),\n",
        "        \"landscape_top\": landscape_top,\n",
        "        \"tumour_vs_normal\": tumour_vs_normal,\n",
        "        \"tp53\": tp53,\n",
        "        \"verdict\": verdict,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    raise NotImplementedError(\"run_analysis\")"
      ]
